  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Starting at the foot of the Notre-Dame-des-Maures track, wide, shaded and little-used forest tracks lead to the largest dolmen in the Var, a Neolithic megalith listed as a Historic Monument. The route also crosses vineyards and offers lovely views over the Îles d'Or, the Giens peninsula and the Massif des Maures.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Allow about 9.3 km for the full loop (~3h), or a short 2.3 km variant if you just want to see the dolmen. The path is easy, with a few moderate climbs, and dogs are welcome on a leash. The massif is often closed from 21 June to 20 September depending on fire risk conditions — remember to check before setting off.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: this shaded, little-used walk is ideal for families, but always check massif access in summer before hitting the road.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>La Londe-les-Maures and its vineyards are just nearby, a good excuse to extend the outing.</p>
    </div>

